Under EU Directive 2000/36/EC
<https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eudr/2000/36/2013-11-18/data.html>,
chocolate makers are permitted to add up to \(5\%\) of specific vegetable
fats (including shea butter) as cocoa butter equivalents. This addition
must not reduce the required minimum cocoa butter or dry cocoa solids, and
it requires prominent, specific labeling. [1
<https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eudr/2000/36/2013-11-18/data.html>, 2
<https://www.confectionerynews.com/Article/2016/10/11/Vegetable-fats-in-cho=
colate-threaten-artisans-says-MEP/>,
3
<https://vespertool.com/blog/is-shea-butter-a-smart-cocoa-butter-substitute=
/>
]
Key Regulations & Requirements

   - *Maximum limit:* The total weight of the added vegetable fats must not
   exceed \(5\%\) of the finished chocolate product's total weight (excludi=
ng
   the weight of any other edible additions like nuts or fruit). [1
   <https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eudr/2000/36/2013-11-18/data.html>]
   - *Approved Fats:* Only six specific, tropical vegetable fats rich in
   symmetrical monounsaturated triglycerides are allowed as cocoa butter
   substitutes:
      - Shea butter
      - Illipe butter (Borneo tallow)
      - Palm oil
      - Sal butter
      - Kokum gurgi
      - Mango kernel [1
      <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=3DCELEX:920=
00E001314>,
      2 <https://www.choc-o-holic.co.uk/chocolate-regulations/>, 3
      <https://www.soci.org/-/media/files/lecture-series/pb129.ashx>, 4
      <https://www.confectionerynews.com/Article/2016/10/11/Vegetable-fats-=
in-chocolate-threaten-artisans-says-MEP/>
      ]
   - *Labeling Rules:* According to Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011
   <https://www.cbi.eu/market-information/natural-food-additives/shea-butte=
r-food/market-entry>,
   manufacturers cannot hide the use of these fats. The packaging must incl=
ude
   a clear, legible, and conspicuous statement on the same field of vision =
as
   the sales name: *"contains vegetable fats in addition to cocoa butter."*
   [1 <https://www.choc-o-holic.co.uk/chocolate-regulations/>, 2
   <https://www.cbi.eu/market-information/natural-food-additives/shea-butte=
r-food/market-entry>
   ]
   - *Quality Standards:* The addition of shea butter cannot substitute or
   reduce the minimum legal thresholds for total dry cocoa solids and cocoa
   butter required for the specific type of chocolate (e.g., minimum \(25\%=
\)
